2026-06-05 20:08:59,663 ['False', 'The user is asking a specific question about whether the methodology in the provided article explicitly references a microaerobic pretreatment method involving the direct injection of limited air into the digester or substrate.\nThe question asks: "Does the methodology explicitly references a microaerobic pretreatment by direct injection of limited air quantity in the anaerobic digester or in the substrate. Specifically, without the inclusion of an additional bacterial consortium or organic material that degrate the substrate under low oxygen conditions?"\nConstraints:\n1. Read only the methodology part of the article.\n2. Answer truthfully based on the methodology text.\n3. No inference/overinterpretation.\n4. Only "true" or "false" as the output format.\n5. Must consider feedstock processing as pretreatment (which the prompt suggests, but specifically asks about the *microaerobic pretreatment by direct injection of limited air* which is a specific condition).\n\nLet\'s look at the "Materials and methods" section (Section 2) and "Introduction" (Section 1) to see what pretreatment techniques are described.\n\nSection 2.2.1 (Microwave pretreatment (MP)): "Microwave pretreatment (MP) was used to liquefy the GMM... The substrate and water ratio taken for the experiments were 1:50... Pretreatment was performed in polytetra fluoro ethylene sealed container with capacity of 500 mL."\nSection 2.2.2 (Surfactant microwave pretreatment (SMP)): "The SMP was carried out with 1:50 ratio of GMM and water were taken in 500 mL container..."\n\nSection 2.3 (Hydrolysis and acidogenesis study): "...The samples were thermally treated at 102 °C at half an hour to restrain the methanogenic microbes. Then pinch of 2 - bromoethyl sulfonic acid (BESA) was introduced in each bottles. Finally, to eliminate the small indefinite amount of oxygen from the bottles, N_2 was passed..."\nWait, the description of the fermentation study in Section 2.3 says: "Hydrolys