pplied to untreated and KOH_Upt WS... All the tests in this study were prepared in triplicates. Two separate bottles with only inoculum (15 g TS⋅L^−1) were also placed in the bath as control. The remaining working volume was filled by adding distilled water. Nitrogen gas was purged to confirm removal of any residual oxygen in bottles. Finally, all the bottles were tightly sealed to maintain anaerobic conditions."\n        *   Here it says "Nitrogen gas was purged... to confirm removal of any residual oxygen... maintain anaerobic conditions."\n        *   This is a standard anaerobic condition description.\n        *   It does *not* describe a specific "microaerobic pretreatment" where air is injected *into* the substrate *before* the digestion process, distinct from the standard batch anaerobic process.\n        *   The question asks about a specific "microaerobic pretreatment" involving direct injection of limited air *before* incorporation in the digestion, without additional bacteria or organic material to degrade substrate under low oxygen.\n        *   The study uses "Alkaline pretreatments coupled with thermal applications" (Sambusiti, Yuan), "Low concentration alkali pretreatment" (Introduction).\n        *   The methodology section for "Anaerobic digestion" (2.3) describes the test setup. It states: "Nitrogen gas was purged... maintain anaerobic conditions." This is the digestion phase.\n        *   The "Pretreatment" section (2.2) describes "Ultrasonic assisted KOH pretreatment".\n        *   Is there a section describing a microaerobic pretreatment? No.\n        *   Is there any mention of injecting air into the *substrate* *before* digestion in the *methods* section? No. The study focuses on "Ultrasonic assisted KOH pretreatment".\n        *   The question asks specifically: "Does the methodology explicitly references a microaerobic pretreatment...?"\n        *   The text mentions "Anaerobic digestion" (2.3) where "Nitrogen gas was purged...". This is sta