erent amounts of NaOH and H2O2". This is chemical pretreatment.\nIs there any mention of injecting air? No, "N2 was injected... up to 5 min". Nitrogen injection creates an anaerobic environment, but not microaerobic.\nIs there any mention of organic material or bacteria? No.\n\nSo, the methodology does not reference a microaerobic pretreatment by injection of air or in the substrate. The pretreatment is chemical.\nTherefore, the answer is False.\n\nWait, I need to check if "NaOH and H2O2" counts as a microaerobic pretreatment? No, it\'s chemical.\nIs there any other part? "co-digestion of products based on the availability of substrates".\n"substrates were firstly co-digested with different NaOH and H2O2 amounts".\n"reactors were pretreated with different amounts of NaOH and H2O2".\nIt seems the only pretreatment is chemical.\nSo the statement that the methodology explicitly references a microaerobic pretreatment is False.\n\nThe user asks to answer ONLY with true or false.\nSo I must output "True" or "False".\n\nConclusion: False. The methodology does not describe microaerobic pretreatment. It describes chemical pretreatment (NaOH/H2O2).']
